[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/5399562549","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/194602#issuecomment-5399562549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/194602","id":5399562549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABQdbJNQ","user":{"login":"quinnarnold","id":218784055,"node_id":"U_kgDODQphNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218784055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold","html_url":"https://github.com/quinnarnold","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnarnold/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T18:26:33Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T18:26:33Z","body":"I traced this against current `main`. I used Codex to help inspect the code-generation and lifetime paths; I reviewed the following analysis and agree with it:\n\n> Scheduler DCE records unused multi-outputs in `V.graph.removed_buffers`, but `generate_c_shim_fallback_kernel` still creates an owning `RAIIAtenTensorHandle` for every required return slot. Removed buffers are excluded from the normal free path, so the unused handle receives no `.reset()` and survives until function return. The original max-pool reproduction is now normally decomposed, but the same behavior remains reproducible with a values-only `topk`.\n\nI propose immediately resetting returned `ir.MultiOutput` handles already present in `V.graph.removed_buffers`, with one CPU cpp-wrapper generated-code regression checking numerical correctness and handle placement. Would that scope be welcome, and could the issue be marked `actionable`?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/5399562549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/5404116138","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/194602#issuecomment-5404116138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/194602","id":5404116138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABQhxEqg","user":{"login":"xpfjmj","id":178886633,"node_id":"U_kgDOCqmX6Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178886633?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj","html_url":"https://github.com/xpfjmj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xpfjmj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T02:07:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T02:07:57Z","body":"Thanks for the analysis! I agree with the proposed scope. Please mark it as actionable. @quinnarnold \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions